(7213581, 1111086, 102278, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Quaint Clive, wouldn''t of thought Matilda was old enough to go to school though, unless you start them early! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, she''s four now and only goes 10-3.30 four days a week and the morning of that is nursery.  It''s not compulsory until 5 or 6 i think. Generally, i''m not a fan of sending kids to school until much later really - i think they start too early - but Matilda loves going and as it''s a small village with only a handful of kids i think she''d miss the company and her friends. It''s all play orientated learning at this age anyway. And it''s Welsh language which will be interesting as she grows up bilingual.</td>', 'Originally posted by Neat: Quaint Clive, wouldn''t of thought Matilda was old enough to go to school though, unless you start them early!   Well, she''s four now and only goes 10-3.30 four days a week and the morning of that is nursery.  It''s not compulsory until 5 or 6 i think. Generally, i''m not a fan of sending kids to school until much later really - i think they start too early - but Matilda loves going and as it''s a small village with only a handful of kids i think she''d miss the company and her friends. It''s all play orientated learning at this age anyway. And it''s Welsh language which will be interesting as she grows up bilingual.', '2014-05-07 05:22:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7213585, 1111086, 102278, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by kiwinick:</b></div><hr/><i> ... but it seems to me to be a grim landscape of a grim place </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Nah, it''s a lovely place in a National Park. It just looks grim at dusk when it''s raining and i''ve obviously chosen to create that mood.</td>', 'Originally posted by kiwinick: ... but it seems to me to be a grim landscape of a grim place   Nah, it''s a lovely place in a National Park. It just looks grim at dusk when it''s raining and i''ve obviously chosen to create that mood.', '2014-05-07 05:24:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(7213588, 1111262, 102278, '<td valign="top">Fantastic clarity. Great shot. Congrats on the Blue. Very well deserved.</td>', 'Fantastic clarity. Great shot. Congrats on the Blue. Very well deserved.', '2014-05-07 05:25:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(7213631, 1111262, 92577, '<td valign="top">Another great addition to your portfolio.  Looked like the winner from the start. Congrats.</td>', 'Another great addition to your portfolio.  Looked like the winner from the start. Congrats.', '2014-05-07 05:53:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(7213634, 1111086, 114285, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rooum:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Neat:</b></div><hr/><i> Quaint Clive, wouldn''t of thought Matilda was old enough to go to school though, unless you start them early! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Well, she''s four now and only goes 10-3.30 four days a week and the morning of that is nursery.  It''s not compulsory until 5 or 6 i think. Generally, i''m not a fan of sending kids to school until much later really - i think they start too early - but Matilda loves going and as it''s a small village with only a handful of kids i think she''d miss the company and her friends. It''s all play orientated learning at this age anyway. And it''s Welsh language which will be interesting as she grows up bilingual. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh Dear, yes time has slipped away, I kind of figured she was still about 3 :)</td>', 'Originally posted by rooum: Originally posted by Neat: Quaint Clive, wouldn''t of thought Matilda was old enough to go to school though, unless you start them early!   Well, she''s four now and only goes 10-3.30 four days a week and the morning of that is nursery.  It''s not compulsory until 5 or 6 i think. Generally, i''m not a fan of sending kids to school until much later really - i think they start too early - but Matilda loves going and as it''s a small village with only a handful of kids i think she''d miss the company and her friends. It''s all play orientated learning at this age anyway. And it''s Welsh language which will be interesting as she grows up bilingual.   Oh Dear, yes time has slipped away, I kind of figured she was still about 3 :)', '2014-05-07 06:52:57.000000', NULL, 0),
